<title>USA: Heartstream adopts shareholder rights plan.</title>
<headline>Heartstream adopts shareholder rights plan.</headline>
<dateline>SEATTLE, Wash. 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Heartstream Inc said on Monday its board of directors has approved a stockholder rights plan and declared a dividend of one preferred share purchase right for each outstanding common share.</p>
<p>The non-taxable distribution will be made on January 6, 1997 to stockholders of record on that date.</p>
<p>If a person or group acquired 15 percent or more of company common, each right would entitle the holder to purchase a number of shares -- at an exercise price currently at $75 -- of common stock with a market value that is twice the right's exercise price.</p>
</text>
